  "corrections": [
    {
      "id": "verified-cache-origin-unavailable",
      "diagnostic": "../cache-boundary-diagnostic.json",
      "change": "Verified cache can satisfy a descriptor despite missing/corrupt origin. Three new cases and an origin-only wrong-solution control. Opaque release identifiers.",
      "exposure": "Artifact generator expanded after original post-selection control exposure; all current artifact controls are regression controls, not fresh holdouts."
    },
    {
      "id": "checker-required-scenario-window-coverage",
      "date": "2026-09-08",
      "change": "A checker-required grading mechanism was added (submissions must include an independently-written checker.mjs, judged against real verdict-stripped traces of the reference/alternative/every control). Building it honestly surfaced a real coverage gap in verified-installation-repair and capacity-maintenance-repair: the reference's own incidental behavior (cache-probing order; the still-buggy starter's early termination) let the scenario-window auto-selector report a control as \"distinguishable\" before its actual planted defect was ever exercised. Both generators' scenario counts were widened (verified-installation-repair 33->44 cases; capacity-maintenance-repair 25->138 cases, via duplicated independently-confirmed witnessing scenarios) so every control's real, declared defect is authoritatively exercised somewhere in the space, not just something that happens to look different. route-policy-repair, rule-index-repair and snapshot-recovery-repair needed no scenario changes for this.",
      "exposure": "Generator bytes changed after the controls listed in validationControls above were already authored/inspected; this is a disclosed re-freeze, not a silent replacement. verified-installation-repair's generator was extended (new cases appended past the prior 33). capacity-maintenance-repair's generator was restructured, not just appended to: duplicated copies of the specific witnessing scenarios were added via cloning loops so the checker-required scenario-window selector reliably lands on them; case ids there are not guaranteed to match the prior freeze's numbering."
    }
  ]
